<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liber Census Daniae</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as King Valdemar's Census Book</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Liber <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/census">Census</a> Daniae, or King Valdemar's Census Book, is a Danish royal land register compiled mainly in the 1230s under Valdemar II. Besides listing royal revenues in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, it contains a survey of the Danish-ruled districts of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, naming villages and their landholders, many of them German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>. It is a key source for medieval Danish and Estonian history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liber-census-daniae.jpg" alt="Liber Census Daniae" width="320" height="292" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl Georg Jensen (1851-1933) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ValdemarSejr_Heraldik.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
